## 3. Code change (the only production edit this session)
- `verify_callback(..., require_effect_pending: bool = True)` + `dispatch_callback` passes
  `require_effect_pending=(verb == "approve")`. **Rationale:** chrono `status=pending` binding is
  required only for `approve` (the sole verb that settles money). `deny`/`later` do not move money and
  must remain usable on a non-pending effect (backcompat + rejecting an expired/settled card). Money
  authorization is UNCHANGED — `approve` still routes through `EffectorGate.release_effect`, which
  re-checks binding + `status='pending'` atomically. (Constitution reason 1; Mission B: expiry+owner+
  action+effect+HMAC checked at callback; canonical chrono release only.)

